#!/usr/bin/env bash
# B4d = B2f with ONE factor changed: + --aug_apm_p 0.6 (WebRTC NS pass on 60% of clips; --aug_apm_ns_levels left at default 6 12 18 21)
#   generated by exploop (wave B4, iteration 4) from exploop/B4/iter04/design.result.json
#  B4d = B2f + --aug_apm_p 0.6. This is the apm_ns dose step and the conditional iteration d of the
#    B4 screen (rdloop B4 module b4wave). Each training clip, of either class, has a 60% chance of
#    one pass through the standalone WebRTC NoiseSuppressor (pywebrtc_audio, NS only, no
#    HPF/AGC/AEC). The pass runs after the acoustic stage and before the codec, from the separate
#    B4 RNG stream. The suppression level is drawn uniformly from the default 6/12/18/21 dB
#    (--aug_apm_ns_levels unchanged). Why: opus_plc (B4b) was null on both readouts, so the
#    pre-registered zero-loss control is not triggered. The analyst's best-supported follow-up is
#    the dose step of B4a, the only positive arm: final +1.02 [+0.43, +1.60], merge +0.57 [-0.01,
#    +1.17] vs B2f. The equally dosed 30% arms B4b (+0.24 / +0.12) and B4c (+0.03 / +0.20) were
#    null. Target: the noisy bona false alarms, the largest remaining error. Half-B noisy FA were
#    B2f 213 / 210 and B4a 192 / 177; mean noisy EER was B2f 10.09 / 9.66 and B4a 9.53 / 9.16. The
#    run should lift the merge readout's CI low above 0. Guards: clean F1 within 0.5, R_spoof
#    within 0.5 on every set, heldout spoof misses <= B4a's 23 / 19, offline-NS spoof misses <= 29.
#    Everything else is B2f's argv: 8 epochs, batch 16, seed 1234.
#  Why: This is iteration d, the conditional last slot of the B4 screen (max_iterations 4). The
#    wave.json lever_notes say: "if opus_plc is 'positive' on the WF1 CI rule, run its
#    pre-registered zero-loss control ... Otherwise pick the best-supported B4 follow-up from the
#    analyst's proposals (B4 flags only)." B4b (opus_plc) is "null (inside +-0.5)" on both readouts
#    (iter02/verdict.json: merge +0.24 [-0.30, +0.78], final +0.12 [-0.48, +0.71]), so the
#    zero-loss control is not triggered. user_notes.md has one note: judge arms on the verdict.json
#    verdicts (B4a: merge revisit, final promote/positive). It does not change the queue. Base =
#    B2f, because rules.keep_best keeps it as the reference for the whole wave. Why the apm_ns dose
#    step (analyst rank 1 in the B4c analyze.result.json): - B4a (`--aug_apm_p 0.3`) is the only B4
#    arm with a positive verdict. iter01/verdict.json gives final 93.15 vs 92.14, delta +1.02, CI
#    [+0.43, +1.60] (positive, promote) and merge 92.55 vs 91.98, delta +0.57, CI [-0.01, +1.17]
#    (above band, CI includes 0). - The two later arms were both null, so they now act as
#    equal-dose placebos for "generic extra 30% DSP augmentation": B4b +0.24 / +0.12 and B4c +0.03
#    / +0.20. The B4a gain is therefore not explained by adding any DSP stage at p 0.3. - B4a's
#    gain sits where the largest remaining error sits, the noisy bona false alarms (B4c report §5.4
#    / largest_remaining_error). Half-B noisy bona FA fell 213 -> 192 (merge) and 210 -> 177
#    (final); saturated FA 136 -> 114 / 133 -> 123; mean noisy EER 10.09 -> 9.53 / 9.66 -> 9.16. It
#    also has the wave's smallest oracle gap (0.43 / 0.10). - The exp-design skill allows a
#    one-flag dose step after a clear positive. The open question for the owner at wrapup is
#    whether B4a's gain is real and dose-responsive, or a single-seed fluctuation whose merge CI
#    touches 0. Doubling p is the one flag-level test of that. Why not the others: - Rank 2,
#    `--aug_apm_ns_levels 18 21` at p 0.3: it chases the secondary afftdn-vs-anlmdn contrast (B4a
#    -1.39 / -1.14, rank 1 of 3). B4a's primary NS contrast is REFUTED on the final (DiD +0.49),
#    and placebo B4c beats it (-0.07, B4c report §2.6). It also leaves open whether the outcome
#    gain itself repeats. - Rank 3, the opus zero-loss control: its pre-registered trigger
#    (opus_plc positive) did not fire, and there is no B4b gain to attribute. - Rank 4,
#    `--aug_dtx_p 1.0`: by the B4c analyst's own account, dose_ratio stays near 0.03
#    ("under-dosed"). B4c also broke the matched R_spoof must-not-move item (-0.69 on both
#    readouts). - Rank 5, the seed repeat: --seed is outside `allowed` (wave seed pinned to 1234),
#    the owner declined a B2f replicate, and configuration levers remain. Constraints: -
#    `--aug_apm_p` is in `allowed`. It is coupled with `--aug_apm_ns_levels`, which stays at its
#    default 6 12 18 21, so this is one factor. - validate_b4_args only requires 0 <= p <= 1. -
#    Nothing forbidden or fixed is touched. num_epochs stays 8 (max 10), batch_size 16, seed 1234.
#    Risks recorded in the B4a report that a higher dose could amplify: - half-B heldout spoof
#    misses 16 -> 23 / 14 -> 19; - heldout English bona recall 56.6 / 58.9; - train loss above
#    B2f's at every epoch (ep8 0.0562 vs 0.0501); - ep1 TrainAcc 86.88 vs 87.36. These are written
#    into the falsifier.
#  Hypothesis: B4a's half-B gain comes from the WebRTC NS pass and grows with exposure. Training
#    both classes on suppressor-processed noisy audio pulls noisy bona out of the movable
#    false-alarm band and puts the operating point at p = 0.5. Equal-dose arms on other DSP slots
#    were null (B4b, B4c), so the effect is specific to the NS pass, not generic augmentation. At p
#    = 0.6 the gain should hold or grow, and the merge CI low should clear 0.
#  Expected signature: Outcome (half_B, vs B2f 91.98 / 92.14): - merge delta > +0.5 with CI low > 0
#    (B4a: +0.57 [-0.01, +1.17]); - final delta >= +0.5 (B4a +1.02); - matched F1 delta >= +1.0 on
#    both readouts (B4a +1.24 / +1.56); - mean noisy EER <= 9.53 / 9.16 (B4a; B2f 10.09 / 9.66); -
#    half-B noisy bona FA <= 192 / 177 (B4a; B2f 213 / 210), with saturated (p >= 0.99) FA below
#    136 / 133; - oracle gap on the final no larger than B4a-top5's 0.43. Mechanism, secondary
#    (b4_dsp_slices.py --lever apm_ns, placebos B4b and B4c; B4a read as the half-dose point): -
#    afftdn-vs-anlmdn DiD more negative than B4a's -1.39 (final) / -1.14 (merge), still rank 1
#    against B4b (-0.36 / -0.22) and B4c (-0.50 / -0.44); - the primary NS-vs-no-NS contrast is not
#    expected to reach 'shown' (B4a REFUTED at +0.49 final). Must not move: - dev_online_clean F1
#    within 0.5 of 97.60 / 97.69; - R_spoof within 0.5 on every set; - full-set offline-NS spoof
#    misses <= 29 (B4a 20 / 15); - half-B noisy spoof misses <= 36 / 35 (B4a 31 / 31); - half-B
#    heldout spoof misses <= B4a's 23 / 19; - ep1 TrainAcc >= 85.36 (B2f 87.36, B4a 86.88); - ep8
#    TrainLoss <= 0.0752. Train log: the wrtc_ns6/12/18/21 counts sum to about 0.6 x 75,785 =
#    45,471 clips per epoch (about 11,368 per level), class-balanced (bona about 8,612, spoof about
#    36,859). No fail_wrtc_ns. Epochs run at most about 1 min longer than B4a's 31 min.
#  Derivation: python3 -I (clip counts per epoch from the B4a report §1: 75,785 = 14,353 bona +
#    61,432 spoof; gpu_h from docs/experiment_log.csv: B2f 4.14, B4a 4.21): p=0.3: expected NS
#    clips/epoch 22736 (bona 4306, spoof 18430); per level (4 levels) 5684 p=0.6: expected NS
#    clips/epoch 45471 (bona 8612, spoof 36859); per level (4 levels) 11368 gpu_h linear in p: B2f
#    4.14 + 2*(B4a 4.21 - B2f) = 4.28 h train; + ~0.5 h eval/analysis = 4.78 h
#  Eval note: This is a screen arm, and B2f stays the reference (rules.keep_best). Compare both
#    readouts (merge_top5, epoch_8) with B2f-top5 / B2f-ep8 on the 17 sls_local17 sets, with the
#    2000-sample bootstrap CI. Also tabulate the dose response p = 0 / 0.3 / 0.6 (B2f / B4a / B4d)
#    on both readouts: - half_B WF1, WF1@oracle and the oracle-gap decomposition; - clean / matched
#    / heldout / echo F1 and R_spoof; - noisy EER; - half-B noisy bona FA and saturated FA (en / zh
#    split); - half-B heldout spoof misses. Mechanism: run scripts/b4_dsp_slices.py --lever apm_ns
#    on merge and final, with --ref = B2f's same readout and --placebo = B4b and B4c. The secondary
#    afftdn-vs-anlmdn contrast is the NS-specific readout; compare it with B4a's -1.39 / -1.14.
#    Check that the run is not ANOMALOUS on the VAD and PLC contrasts. Watch: - heldout English
#    bona recall (B4a half-B 56.6 / 58.9); - heldout spoof misses (B4a 23 / 19); - matched R_spoof;
#    - ep1 TrainAcc and the per-epoch train-loss gap to B2f; - the wrtc_ns6/12/18/21 counts
#    (~45,471 per epoch) and fail_wrtc_ns in train.log. This is the last iteration of the wave; the
#    SUMMARY follows.
#  Falsification (pre-registered): delta top-5-merge half_B.wf1.wf1 vs B2f merge (91.98) > +0.5
#    with the paired-bootstrap CI excluding 0 and clean F1 drop <= 0.5 -> positive; within +-0.5 ->
#    null; below -0.5 -> negative. (1) No dose response: a final delta vs B2f < +0.5, or a merge
#    delta below B4a's +0.57 together with a final below B4a's +1.02 by more than the ±0.5 band.
#    Either means B4a's gain was not dose-driven (or was seed noise); close the flag-level apm_ns
#    line and do not promote B4a without a seed replicate. (2) Trade-off: half-B heldout spoof
#    misses above B4a's 23 / 19, matched or heldout R_spoof down > 0.5, or full-set offline-NS
#    spoof misses > 29. More NS buys bona recall with spoof recall ('NS => bona'); drop the higher
#    dose. (3) Lost raw-noise exposure: WF1 delta < -0.5 with matched F1 down > 1.0 vs B2f; drop.
#    (4) Clean guard: dev_online_clean F1 down > 0.5; drop. (5) Shared under-fit: ep1 TrainAcc <
#    85.36 or ep8 TrainLoss > 0.0752, together with heldout bona recall down; confounded. (6)
#    Mechanism (secondary): afftdn-vs-anlmdn DiD > -0.84 (the panel mean) on the final; the
#    harsh-suppressor signal does not scale with dose. Verdict rule (wave): positive = merge half_B
#    WF1 delta > +0.5 with CI low > 0 and clean drop <= 0.5; |delta| <= 0.5 = null.
#
#   bash scripts/run_B4d.sh                                   # fresh run (the exploop supervisor launches it)
#   bash scripts/run_B4d.sh --resume exp/<run dir name>       # after a container restart
#   EXPLOOP_PRINT_ARGV=1 bash scripts/run_B4d.sh              # print the trainer argv, launch nothing
#
# Rendered from scripts/exploop/launcher_template.sh (same shape as scripts/run_B3a.sh). Extra
# arguments are appended to the trainer command line. Training runs under nohup; stdout/stderr go to
# <workdir>/<track>_<timestamp>.log and the per-epoch summary to <run dir>/logs/train.log.
set -euo pipefail

PY="${PY:-/root/.conda/envs/rtc-sdd/bin/python}"
TRACK="B4d_qwen17_rtc_musan_loud23_cos8_lr2.5e6_apmns06_s1234"
WORKDIR="/root/repos/rtc-sdd/Ghostbusters_team/SLS_setup"

ARGS=(
    --train_data_path /mnt/paml-research/RTCFake/data/wav/train
    --train_protocol /mnt/paml-research/RTCFake/data/train_label.txt
    --dev_data_path /mnt/paml-research/RTCFake/data/wav/dev
    --dev_protocol ../data/dev_noisy_sim/dev_label_excl_halfB.txt
    --ssl_name Qwen/Qwen3-ASR-1.7B
    --n_layers 24
    --batch_size 16
    --num_epochs 8
    --num_workers 64
    --use_rtc_aug
    --aug_noise_dirs ../data/augmentation_train/rnnoise ../data/augmentation_train/esc50
    --aug_rir_dirs ../data/augmentation_train/rirs
    --musan
    --musan_dir ../data/augmentation/musan
    --loudness_norm
    --loudness_norm_lufs -23
    --optim adamw
    --lr 2.5e-6
    --head_lr_mult 10
    --weight_decay 0.01
    --lr_scheduler warmup_cosine
    --warmup_frac 0.05
    --lr_min 5e-7
    --grad_clip 1.0
    --ema_decay 0.9995
    --local_eval_sets ../configs/local_eval_sets.yaml
    --earlystop_metric wf1
    --earlystop_epoch 99
    --keep_topk_by_wf1 7
    --keep_epochs 8
    --seed 1234
    --track "$TRACK"
    --aug_apm_p 0.6
)

if [ "${EXPLOOP_PRINT_ARGV:-0}" = "1" ]; then
    printf '%s\n' "${ARGS[@]}"
    exit 0
fi

if [ ! -x "$PY" ]; then
    echo "python not found: $PY (set PY=... to override)" >&2
    exit 1
fi
if ! command -v ffmpeg >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "ffmpeg not found on PATH: the RTC codec augmentation would silently no-op. Reinstall it first." >&2
    exit 1
fi
if ! "$PY" -c "import pyloudnorm" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "pyloudnorm not importable by $PY: run '$PY -m pip install pyloudnorm==0.2.0' first." >&2
    exit 1
fi

cd "$WORKDIR"
LOG="${TRACK}_$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S).log"

nohup "$PY" -u -m b4wave.train "${ARGS[@]}" "$@" > "$LOG" 2>&1 &

PID=$!
echo "Started $TRACK (pid $PID)"
echo "Log:     $WORKDIR/$LOG"
echo "Follow:  tail -f $WORKDIR/$LOG"
echo "Stop:    kill $PID"
